{"text": "Lesson four, pillar one, architectural foundations. This pillar changes the model itself. Every family here either deletes the cache, shrinks it, sparsifies access to it, or hybridizes so recall survives. The bill is always recall. Softmax attention keeps a lossless history, one key and one value per token. You can point at a single buried fact. The cost is a cache that scales with length. Subquadratic mixers replace that history with a fixed size state. Linear attention drops the softmax and factors the mixer through a feature map. A summary matrix replaces the cache and updates independent of length. The persistent failure is recall. One summary cannot remember arbitrary content. State space models take the other route. Mamba makes the recurrence selective. The transition depends on the current input. The state has fixed size, so decoding is constant time per step. A hardware-aware scan keeps training competitive. Mamba2 unifies state-space models with linear attention. RWKV arrives at a similar recurrent mixer from the transformer side. Aurora and colleagues make the trade-off explicit. On associative retrieval, recall tracks state size almost monotonically. No fixed state model in the survey has matched softmax on heavy in-context retrieval. Hybrids are the compromise. Keep a few real attention layers among many cheap ones. Jamba uses about one attention layer for every seven Mamba layers, plus mixture of experts. The cache then exists only on the attention layers. Mixture of experts cuts per-token compute, not per-token state. A router sends each token to a few experts, so activated parameters split from total parameters. All experts must still live somewhere. DeepSeek scales to hundreds of billions of total parameters with only tens of billions activated. Even inside a normal transformer, the cache can shrink. Multi-query attention uses one key You head and loses quality. Grouped query attention is the production default. Latent attention stores a small code and rebuilds keys and values. Eviction drops tokens that future attention will not use. What this pillar buys: capacity and bandwidth, more concurrent users, and faster single-stream decode. The price is the recall efficiency frontier, which the survey leaves open.", "language": "en", "duration": 143.088, "words": [{"text": "Lesson", "start": 0.16, "end": 0.46}, {"text": "four,", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.86}, {"text": "pillar", "start": 1.44, "end": 1.721}, {"text": "one,", "start": 1.861, "end": 2.081}, {"text": "architectural", "start": 2.561, "end": 3.181}, {"text": "foundations.", "start": 3.221, "end": 3.981}, {"text": "This", "start": 4.622, "end": 4.782}, {"text": "pillar", "start": 4.862, "end": 5.122}, {"text": "changes", "start": 5.202, "end": 5.562}, {"text": "the", "start": 5.602, "end": 5.682}, {"text": "model", "start": 5.722, "end": 5.982}, {"text": "itself.", "start": 6.022, "end": 6.462}, {"text": "Every", "start": 7.142, "end": 7.382}, {"text": "family", "start": 7.482, "end": 7.823}, {"text": "here", "start": 7.883, "end": 8.103}, {"text": "either", "start": 8.203, "end": 8.383}, {"text": "deletes", "start": 8.443, "end": 8.803}, {"text": "the", "start": 8.823, "end": 8.903}, {"text": "cache,", "start": 8.943, "end": 9.383}, {"text": "shrinks", "start": 9.763, "end": 10.123}, {"text": "it,", "start": 10.183, "end": 10.303}, {"text": "sparsifies", "start": 10.764, "end": 11.484}, {"text": "access", "start": 11.584, "end": 11.964}, {"text": "to", "start": 12.024, "end": 12.104}, {"text": "it,", "start": 12.204, "end": 12.304}, {"text": "or", "start": 12.704, "end": 12.784}, {"text": "hybridizes", "start": 12.844, "end": 13.545}, {"text": "so", "start": 13.605, "end": 13.685}, {"text": "recall", "start": 13.825, "end": 14.165}, {"text": "survives.", "start": 14.245, "end": 14.805}, {"text": "The", "start": 15.405, "end": 15.485}, {"text": "bill", "start": 15.525, "end": 15.725}, {"text": "is", "start": 15.785, "end": 15.865}, {"text": "always